<title>USA: TABLE - Core Materials Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Core Materials Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>CORE MATERIALS CORP</p>
<p>			  Income Statement Data (unaudited):</p>
<p>			 (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			  Three Months Ended	Six Months Ended</p>
<p>			   6/30/97  6/30/96(1)  6/30/97  6/30/96(1)</p>
<p> Net Sales	     $ 16,659 $ 14,758    $ 33,032   $ 30,703</p>
<p> Costs and Expenses    14,818   14,107	29,619     28,858</p>
<p>Net Income Before</p>
<p>Interest</p>
<p>  and Taxes		 1,841	651	 3,413	1,845</p>
<p> Net Income(a)		766	147	 1,371	  614</p>
<p>Net Income per</p>
<p>  Common Share(a)	  0.08     0.01	  0.14	 0.06</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number</p>
<p>of Common Shares and</p>
<p>Common Stock</p>
<p>  Equivalents	     9,749    9,654	 9,716	9,654</p>
<p>(1) Proforma (a) If the benefit of the company's operating tax loss carryforwards were recorded as a reduction in income tax expense, the company's net income for the three months ended 6/30/97 and 1996 would have been $1,163,000, or $0.12 per share, and $244,000, or $0.02 per share, respectively. For the six months ended 6/30/97 and 1996, net income would have been $2,086,000, or $.22 per share, and $963,000, or $.10 per share, respectively.</p>
